# AGILE TEAM CHARTER 

## 1. Purpose & Vision
The purpose of the internship is for interns to gain prcatical skills in software testing and automation by designing , implementing and maintaining reliable , scalable and maintainable automated testing solutions. 
The mission is to bridge the gap between manual testing and automated quality assurance by developing behaviour-driven development frameworks and performance solutions under the guidance of the internship mentor.

## 2. Roles and Responsibilities
Dante Swartz - Internship Mentor - Provides technical guidance, communicates expectations, defines acceptance criteria, reviews work, facilitates meetings and approves completed deliverables.
Interns - Complete assigned tasks, develop automation scripts, manages Git feature branches, executes tests, documents results. 

## 3. Ways of working 
## 3.1 Agile Approach
The team applies scrum for planning and regular reviews of the work.

## 3.2 Team Ceremonies
**Daily Stand-up** - Occurs daily for approximately 15 minutes. The purpose is to share work, plan activities and report any blockers. 
**Demonstration** - This occurs at the end of a sprint. The purpose is to demonstrate completed work.
**Retrospective** - Occurs at the end of a sprint to reflect on the progress, challenges and technical learning .

## 4. Working Agreements
1. Attend daily stand-ups an dmentor meetings on time 
2.Communicate blockers and technical difficulties as early as possible.
3. Follow agreed coding standards and mantain clear, readable code.
4. Use GitLab feature branches and Merge Requests to manage code changes. 
5. Collaborate with each other effectively.

## 5. Communication
## 5.1 Communication Channels
1. Microsoft Teams: Daily communication, progress updates.
2. GitLab: Source control, issue tracking and Merge Requests and code reviews.
3. Email: Formal communication and important programme updates.

## 5.2 Remote Working 
Team members are expected to remain contactable during working hours. Camera use is mandatory during daily stand-ups.

## 6. Decision-Making 
The team encourages collaboration and discussion when making technical decisions. Interns may propose and discuss implementation approaches, while the mentor has the final decision on programme requirements, coding standards, acceptance criteria and final deliverable approval.

## 7. Definition of Done 
1. Code completed and reviewed
2. All tests passed 
3. Documentation updated

## 8. Core values and behaviours 
1. Respect
2. Transparency 
3. Accountability .
